          <p><em><strong>Vilhelm Hammersh=C3=B8i: Pictures from Home</stron=
g></em><br>November 11, 2027 to February 14, 2028</p><p>The first major Nor=
th American exhibition devoted to Vilhelm Hammersh=C3=B8i=E2=80=99s work in=
 more than a decade, this show will focus on the artist=E2=80=99s most cele=
brated paintings=E2=80=94his series of enigmatic, evocative, and meticulous=
ly observed views of the interior of his apartment at Strandgade 30 in Cope=
nhagen. Central themes of the show include the artist=E2=80=99s manipulatio=
n of spatial ambiguity; his handling of light, shadow, and temporality; the=
 shifting presence of household objects as they migrated between rooms; and=
 the role of his wife, Ida, as the sole figure featured in several composit=
ions. This exhibition is co-organized by the Art Institute of Chicago and T=
he Frick Collection, New York.</p><p><a class=3D"frickbutton mx-0 mb-0" hre=
f=3D"https://www.frick.org/exhibitions/hammershoi">Read More<span class=3D"=
